    "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nKeeps the MLA `linear_q_proj` that the layer spec asks for when `q_lora_rank` is `None` and `qk_layernorm` is on, instead of always replacing it with a fused norm+linear.\n\nSince #4452, `QKNormConfigResolver._resolve_mla_qk_layernorm` swaps `linear_q_proj` for `backend.column_parallel_layer_norm_linear()` whenever there is no Q-LoRA, although the GPT layer specs pass `backend.column_parallel_linear()`. That adds an RMSNorm on the Q path (`linear_q_proj.layer_norm_weight`) that MLA models without Q-LoRA do not have; in DeepSeek-V2-Lite and Sarvam 105B the query is `q_proj(hidden_states)`. Up to `core_r0.18.0` the projection was plain. With the fused default, Megatron-Bridge cannot import such Hugging Face checkpoints (the norm has no source weight), and models trained from scratch get a Q norm that their inference implementations lack.\n\nA spec that selects the fused norm+linear for `linear_q_proj` still gets the Q norm, as the message in `_raise_unused_q_norm` already suggests. The KV path is unchanged.\n\nTesting: `tests/unit_tests/transformer/test_mla_qk_norm_config.py` fails on `main` and passes with this change. `tests/unit_tests/transformer/test_multi_latent_attention.py` gives the same results with and without this change on one GPU. A small Sarvam MLA model imported through Megatron-Bridge with a plain `linear_q_proj` matches the Hugging Face logits (relative L2 difference 5e-4 in FP32).\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: related to NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge#5261. Megatron-Bridge works around this for DeepSeek with an `MLASelfAttention` subclass (NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge#5262); other MLA models without Q-LoRA, such as Moonlight and Sarvam 105B, still get the extra Q norm.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] If this PR adds or changes a GPU kernel (Triton, `jit_fuser`/`torch.compile`, CUDA extension, TE or external-library dispatch, or a scatter/index accumulation), I have added or updated its bit-exact determinism test and registered it in `tests/unit_tests/determinism/kernels/manifest.py` ([guide](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/docs/developer/determinism/testing.md))\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code [Typing guidelines](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html)\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [ ] I have run the [autoformatter.sh](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/tools/autoformat.sh) on my PR\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
