        "login": "pushkar-sarvam"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "hey @guihong-nv @janEbert, just bringing this to the top - can you have a look at the PR?",
      "created_at": "2026-10-19T15:18:21Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/7973#issuecomment-6270705751",
      "id": 6270705751,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-19T15:18:21Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "pushkar-sarvam"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "I think this is quite difficult. On the one hand, it's correct that Q also gets a norm when a setting called `qk_layernorm` is set by the user. On the other, it changes the existing default and is an extension that's not specified in the paper.\r\n\r\nI would argue that it's more correct to give a Q norm when it's asked for (`qk_layernorm=True`) rather than just ignoring the setting like it used to (the behavior this PR would revert back to). Subjectively, I'd say it's correct that we add norm support for `q_proj` and that Megatron-Bridge works around this for HF support.\r\n\r\nUnless there's a mathematical reason that having `q_proj` with a norm doesn't make sense?",
      "created_at": "2026-10-19T16:57:01Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/7973#issuecomment-6272567806",
      "id": 6272567806,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-19T16:58:30Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "janEbert"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Feel free to let me know if you disagree. I'll close this for now so we don't accidentally merge.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-19T16:57:53Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/7973#issuecomment-6272584415",
      "id": 6272584415,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-19T16:58:03Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "janEbert"
      }
    }
